<div class="justText">
<ul id="faq" class="faq">
    <li>
        <div class="qContain">
            <span class="faqq"><img src="../images/q.png?v=2" alt="Q" class="Q"> How do I check a load?</span>
            <div class="faqa"><img src="../images/a.png?v=2" alt="A" class="A"> On the <b class="bb"><a href="/" title="Home">Home</a></b> page click <b class="bb">New Load</b> to start.  Then select the type of load; <b class="bb">Round Trip</b>, <b class="bb">One Way</b>, <b class="bb">Pre load</b>, or <b class="bb">Trainer</b>. Start at the top of the page an work your way to the bottom selecting the correct options for the load.  When everything matches for the load pulled click <b class="bb">Done</b> and the load pay will display on the main page.</div>
        </div>
    </li>
    <li>
        <div class="qContain">
            <span class="faqq"><img src="../images/q.png?v=2" alt="Q" class="Q"> How do I track a load?</span>
            <div class="faqa"><img src="../images/a.png?v=2" alt="A" class="A"> After entering the load into the main page, click on the footprints <img src="../images/footprints.png" class="tracking"> located to the right of the load number. This brings you to the Tracking &amp; Overview page.  Enter the load number and any notes you may want to doccument regarding the load and press <b class="bb">Done</b>.</div>
        </div>
    </li>
    <li>
        <div class="qContain">
            <span class="faqq"><img src="../images/q.png?v=2" alt="Q" class="Q"> How do I delete a tracked load?</span>
            <div class="faqa"><img src="../images/a.png?v=2" alt="A" class="A"> After a load has been tracked, it will display an <img src="../images/x.png" border="0" alt="X" width="15px" height="15px" /> to the right of the load.  Clicking this will bring you to a delete page.  You must confirm the deletion of any load, this is done by typing the word &quot;Delete&quot; into the field and pressing <b class="bb">Confirm</b>.  If the load being deleted is associated with the &quot;Last Load&quot; the page will display a warning about the removal of the &quot;Longhaul Differential <span class="moneyDisplay">$40.00</span>&quot; from the database.</div>
        </div>
    </li>
    <li>
        <div class="qContain">
            <span class="faqq"><img src="../images/q.png?v=2" alt="Q" class="Q"> How do I reconcile my pay?</span>
            <div class="faqa"><img src="../images/a.png?v=2" alt="A" class="A"> After the weeks pay has been posted to the HR website you can logon and check the loads against PayTracker to ensure you have been paid correctly.  To do this you need a computer and your phone or a printout from the office of your pay.  On PayTracker, click on &quot;Reconcile&quot; and a list of your oldest, unpaid, loads will display.  Each load is displayed in an individual box with a breakdown of each pay category, proceded by a checked box.  Go down the reconcile page, one load at a time and compare that to your pay sheet, ensuring that each pay item for a specific load was paid correctly. (<em>On Windows or Linux you can press &quot;Ctrl+F&quot;, on a Mac press &quot;Command-F&quot; to bring up a search box, typing the load number in the box will highlight that load on the screen</em>)  The site assumes that everything for that load was paid correctly, defaulting to every paid item being pre-checked.  If this is true, click the <img src="../images/thumbs_up.png" alt="Thumbs Up" height="20px" width="20px"> to mark the load paid, continue this until all loads for that pay period are checked against the pay sheet and marked paid.  If you come across a situation where an item wasn't paid coreectly or at all, uncheck the box next to the item prior to marking it paid and that load will remain, indicating the unpaid portion.  Contact your manager to inform them of the discrepancy, if the pay is corrected on a later pay sheet, you can subsequently mark it paid at a later time.  If you need to change the status of a load that has been marked paid, you can click the <img src="../images/undo.png" alt="Undo" height="20px" width="20px"> button in the top right corner, this displays the most recient loads that have been marked paid.  By clicking the <img src="../images/thumbs_netural.png" alt="Thumbs Netural" height="20px" width="20px"> you will mark that load as &quot;unpaid&quot;.</div>
        </div>
    </li>
    <li>
        <div class="qContain">
            <span class="faqq"><img src="../images/q.png?v=2" alt="Q" class="Q"> How do I change my E-Mail Address?</span>
            <div class="faqa"><img src="../images/a.png?v=2" alt="A" class="A"> On the <a href="../pro/account.php" title="Account">Account</a> page, simply fill in the &quot;Change Email Address&quot; form with your current password and the new email address you wish to use then click <b class="bb">Change Email Address</b>.  A confirmation email will be sent to the new address, you will need to click on the link provided in this email to complete the change.</div>
        </div>
    </li>
    <li>
        <div class="qContain">
            <span class="faqq"><img src="../images/q.png?v=2" alt="Q" class="Q"> How do I change my Password?</span>
            <div class="faqa"><img src="../images/a.png?v=2" alt="A" class="A"> On the <a href="../pro/account.php" title="Account">Account</a> page, in the &quot;Change Password&quot; area click <b class="bb">Reset Password</b>.  A password reset email will be sent to the email address on file, you will need to click on the link provided in this email to complete the change.  Because of the way passwords are stored encrypted in our database, no administrator can view or change a password.  This must be done through the reset password method.</div>
        </div>
    </li>
    <li>
        <div class="qContain">
            <span class="faqq"><img src="../images/q.png?v=2" alt="Q" class="Q"> How do I add more time to my Pro account?</span>
            <div class="faqa"><img src="../images/a.png?v=2" alt="A" class="A"> On the <a href="../pro/account.php" title="Account">Account</a> page, simply tap "Add Time" at the top of the page. Select the amount of time you wish to add. You will be presented with a PayPal button which will allow you to process a payment and once complete the time will be automatically added to your account.</div>
        </div>
    </li>
    <li>
        <div class="qContain">
            <span class="faqq"><img src="../images/q.png?v=2" alt="Q" class="Q"> How do I close or delete my account?</span>
            <div class="faqa"><img src="../images/a.png?v=2" alt="A" class="A"> On the <a href="../pro/account.php" title="Account">Account</a> page, simply click the "Delete Account" button at the bottom of the page. Once the account has been deleted <strong><u>no data will be recoverable and no refunds will be given for unused time.</u></strong></div>
        </div>
    </li>
    <li>
        <div class="qContain">
            <span class="faqq"><img src="../images/q.png?v=2" alt="Q" class="Q"> Can I get a refund if I close my account?</span>
            <div class="faqa"><img src="../images/a.png?v=2" alt="A" class="A"> Unfortunately, no refunds will be given for unused time.</div>
        </div>
    </li>
    <li>
        <div class="qContain">
            <span class="faqq"><img src="../images/q.png?v=2" alt="Q" class="Q"> Can I still use PayTracker if I close my account?</span>
            <div class="faqa"><img src="../images/a.png?v=2" alt="A" class="A"> Yes! The free site will continue to be available but you will lose access to all the pro features. </div>
        </div>
    </li>
    <li>
        <div class="qContain">
            <span class="faqq"><img src="../images/q.png?v=2" alt="Q" class="Q"> Do you have a tutorial video I can watch?</span>
            <div class="faqa"><img src="../images/a.png?v=2" alt="A" class="A"> Yes! I put together a quick video available <a href="../tutorial.php" target="_self">Here</a>. </div>
        </div>
    </li>
</ul>
</div>
